-- title:
--   Counting: $(n-1)^2$ gauge qubits, $2(n-1)$ stabilizer generators, one logical qubit
-- statement:
--   Let $n\ge1$. Counting Pauli operators modulo phase:
--
--   1. $|\mathcal T| = 4^{(n-1)^2}\,|\mathcal S|$;
--   2. $|\mathcal S| = 4^{\,n-1}$;
--   3. $|C(\mathcal S)| = 4\,|\mathcal T|$, where $C(\mathcal S)$ is the set of Pauli operators commuting with $\mathcal S$.
--
--   In the stabilizer formalism these counts say that the $2(n-1)$ generators of $\mathcal S$ are independent, that $\mathcal T$ carries $(n-1)^2$ gauge qubits (the subsystem $\mathcal H^{\mathcal T}$ of dimension $2^{(n-1)^2}$), and that one qubit is encoded (the subsystem $\mathcal H^{\mathcal L}$ of dimension $2$). Together they account for $n^2 = 2(n-1) + (n-1)^2 + 1$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: lattice size n, rows and columns indexed 1..n, generators indexed by Z_{n−1} → n = m + 1 with m : ℕ; rows and columns Fin (m + 1), 0-based; generators indexed by Fin m acting on i.castSucc, i.succ; reason: Lean convention; n = 0 has no qubits, so every lattice of the paper is an instance
--   - encoding: Pauli operators with phases ±1, ±i (the (−1)^φ of (8), (13)) → pairs (a, b) of bit matrices modulo phase; multiplication is addition, commutation is the symplectic bit symp; reason: membership in T, S, C(S), commutation and weight do not depend on the phase
--   - reading: S as the set (10): ⊕_i(∧_j a_ij) = 0, ⊕_j(∧_i b_ij) = 0 → S = the group generated by S^X_i, S^Z_j of (11) (SGroup m); reason: (10) taken alone admits non-full rows (n = 2: a single X_{1,1} satisfies it but anticommutes with Z_{1,1}Z_{1,2} ∈ T, contrary to p.4); the prose before (10) and the generators (11) agree, and S_props proves that the span equals the prose set
--   - reading: dimensions 2^{(n−1)²} and 2 of the tensor factors H^T, H^L, justified by "the stabilizer formalism" → the stabilizer counts |T| = 4^{(n−1)²}|S|, |S| = 4^{n−1}, |C(S)| = 4|T|; reason: the paper derives the dimensions from these counts; (19), the explicit gauge operators, is garbled and not used
-- source:
--   D. Bacon, Operator Quantum Error Correcting Subsystems for Self-Correcting Quantum Memories, arXiv:quant-ph/0506023v4, §IV.B, p.6, after (18)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_BaconOQEC_InT
import Definitions.Def_BaconOQEC_InCS
import Definitions.Def_BaconOQEC_SGroup

namespace BaconOQEC

/-- Bacon, *Operator Quantum Error Correcting Subsystems for Self-Correcting Quantum Memories*,
arXiv:quant-ph/0506023v4, §IV.B, p.6, after (18): "Here we have assigned dimensions 2^{(n−1)²} and
2 to these tensor product spaces. To see why these dimensionalities arise we appeal to the
stabilizer formalism. We note that modulo the stabilizer structure of S, L is a single encoded
qubit." In stabilizer counting (Pauli operators modulo phase):
1. `|T| = 4^{(n−1)²} |S|`: `(n − 1)²` gauge qubits, the subsystem `H^T` of dimension `2^{(n−1)²}`;
2. `|S| = 4^{n−1}`: `2(n − 1)` independent stabilizer generators;
3. `|C(S)| = 4 |T|`, `C(S)` the operators commuting with `S`: one encoded qubit, the subsystem `H^L`
   of dimension `2`.

**Formalization Note.** Indices are 0-based (`Fin (m + 1)`, lattice size `n = m + 1`, so `n ≥ 1`); Pauli operators
modulo phase are pairs `(a, b)` of bit matrices; `|T|` counts the pairs with `InT`, `|S|` the elements of the span
`SGroup m`, `|C(S)|` the pairs with `InCS`. The three counts account for
`n² = 2(n − 1) + (n − 1)² + 1`. Clause 3 is also clause 1 of the goal theorem. -/
theorem card_T_S (m : ℕ) :
    Nat.card {v : Bits m × Bits m // InT v.1 v.2} = 4 ^ (m ^ 2) * Nat.card (SGroup m) ∧
    Nat.card (SGroup m) = 4 ^ m ∧
    Nat.card {v : Bits m × Bits m // InCS v.1 v.2} =
      4 * Nat.card {v : Bits m × Bits m // InT v.1 v.2} := by sorry

end BaconOQEC
